# 5. The Final Two Ideas

## Our Top Two Ideas

### 1. Strata

Document-processing teams often send every page through expensive processing, even when simpler methods like text extraction or OCR would be enough. **Strata** routes each document page to the cheapest engine that can meet the required quality threshold, escalating to more expensive processing only when necessary. AI teams and developers building products that process large volumes of documents would care because processing costs can add up quickly, while routing decisions can also affect accuracy and latency.

### 2. ClientProof

Small web studios often depend on clients to provide website descriptions, images, and other information before a project can be completed. That information is usually scattered across emails, messages, documents, and other files, and missing answers can create delays and repeated clarification rounds. **ClientProof** would help studios collect and organize the material they need, while making it easier for clients to provide the information required to move a project forward.

